From 0217e457db861cd676a9558266f0e204e31b503a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:52:41 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] arm64: dts: exynos: gtactive3wifi: Keep the panel node
 from blocking simpledrm

The framebuffer's "panel" phandle is parsed by fw_devlink (parse_panel
in drivers/of/property.c), so it becomes a supplier link from the
framebuffer to /panel. /panel has no compatible and no parent device,
so it never gets a struct device and is never marked NOT_DEVICE:
fw_devlink_create_devlink() keeps returning -EAGAIN and simpledrm
defers with "wait for supplier /panel". With CONFIG_MODULES=y and
CONFIG_DRIVER_DEFERRED_PROBE_TIMEOUT=0, fw_devlink_probing_done() never
runs, so it would stay deferred and the console would be lost.

of_link_to_phandle() skips suppliers that are not available, while
simpledrm reads width-mm, height-mm and rotation through
of_parse_phandle() regardless of the status. Disable the node.

Fixes: 6ebe9ae81aa1 ("arm64: dts: exynos: gtactive3wifi: Describe the boot framebuffer for simpledrm")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts
index 1943aeec2..51a746fde 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts
@@ -48,8 +48,15 @@ framebuffer0: framebuffer-0 {
 	 * panel and this node only describes it for simpledrm (physical size,
 	 * mounting) and links the DCS backlight. Change "rotation" here if
 	 * userspace should treat another edge as the top.
+	 *
+	 * The node is disabled on purpose: "panel" is a fw_devlink supplier
+	 * property, and an enabled node that never becomes a device would
+	 * keep simpledrm in deferred probe forever ("wait for supplier
+	 * /panel"; this config has no deferred probe timeout). simpledrm
+	 * reads width-mm/height-mm/rotation regardless of the status.
 	 */
 	panel: panel {
+		status = "disabled";
 		width-mm = <108>;
 		height-mm = <172>;
 		rotation = <0>;
-- 
